From: Prarit Bhargava <prarit@redhat.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:05:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Bump OpenTelemetry-Go modules to v1.47.0 for CVE-2026-128085

go-vendor-tools.toml's [archive] pre_commands bumps the OpenTelemetry-Go
modules (otel, otel/metric, otel/sdk, otel/trace, otlptrace,
otlptracegrpc and otlptracehttp) to v1.47.0 before the vendor archive is
generated, but that only ever runs against the vendor checkout, never
against the plain source tarball (Source0). Mirror the same go.mod/go.sum
result into the %prep source tree so go build -mod=vendor does not reject
the build as inconsistent vendoring.

Computed via a real go get of those modules against the prometheus v3.13.5
source after Patch5 and Patch6, then go mod tidy (not hand-edited). The new
exporter releases also raise go-openapi/swag (and its sub-modules) to
v0.28.0, grpc-gateway to v2.30.0, grpc to v1.83.2 and other transitive
modules; go.mod/go.sum match the regenerated vendor archive exactly.

Upstream: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/releases/tag/v1.47.0

CVE-2026-128085: OpenTelemetry-Go attribute truncation bypass in otel/sdk,
otel/trace and otel prior to v1.47.0.

HUM-12704
